  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "deltaTime is a pretty basic thing that most unity games use for physics, movement, pretty much anything under the sun for non-static objects that move. For those who don't know why this would be good, it means that even if your framerate slows down, you'll continue to move at the same uniform speed. In the current version, a player at 45 fps will run/walk slower than those at 90 fps. This is because the game's code is updating by the frame as opposed to following deltaTime, which opperates independent of framerate. \n\n(This post is based off of my observations of how players move at varying framrates, feel free to correct me if you are using deltaTime and something else is causing the slowdown, would genuinely like to know what it is).",
